  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Utah has $6.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Utah recorded 9,832 awards during the period, with an average award size of $618K. Utah obligations are up 16.3% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows obligations moving from $4B in FY21 to $6.1B in FY26, with interim totals of $5.3B in FY22, $6.3B in FY23, $7.2B in FY24, and $5.2B in FY25. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Utah, with $4.4B in obligations this fiscal year to date. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations, accounting for $2.9B. The vendor list is concentrated among several large defense and manufacturing firms: NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP leads with $2.9B, followed by ASAHI REFINING USA INC with $592M and L3 TECHNOLOGIES, INC. with $321M. These figures are contract obligations and reflect fiscal year to date totals, which are partial for the current year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers in Utah this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $4.4B in Utah in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury obligated $654M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $330M. The Departments of Agriculture, Homeland Security, and the General Services Administration follow with $153M, $97.4M, and $93.1M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors capture the most federal spending in Utah?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing attracted $2.9B in obligations. Nonferrous Metal (except Copper and Aluminum) Rolling, Drawing, and Extruding attracted $592M, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction attracted $315M. NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORP received $2.9B, ASAHI REFINING USA INC received $592M, and L3 TECHNOLOGIES, INC. received $321M."
      }
    ]
  },
